Hexagon HTP: one weight stream for the 2 to 4 rows of a verify step (Q4_0 and Q8_0)

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9, with the patches of the series before this one applied.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-mm-kernels-tiled.h  the compact activation and the multi-row dots
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/matmul-ops.h            the kernel type and its VTCM layout
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/matmul-ops.c            the multi-row job, its quantizer, the selection
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp            GGML_HEXAGON_MULTIROW and the kernel type
    tests/test-backend-ops.cpp                        MUL_MAT of 1 to 4 rows at the shapes of the models

A decode step of one token reads every weight of the model from DDR, thus the two product models
run at the bandwidth limit. A verify step of speculative decoding computes 1 + n_draft tokens, and
it must read the weights once for all of them.

The matmul operator had a kernel for one activation row and a kernel for a row pair. Three rows
cost a row pair and a row, and four rows cost two row pairs, because each call reads the weight
tile again from VTCM and prepares it again. The lab of tools/htp-lab measures a Q4_0 tile of 32
rows by 32 k values at 70.8 cycles for one row, 100.7 for two, 171.4 for three and 201.3 for four.

This patch adds a dot for 1 to 4 rows that prepares the weights of a k-tile once and keeps one
accumulator per row. The rows take their activation from a compact copy in DDR through scalar
registers, with vrmpy(Vu.ub, Rt.b), thus each more row costs the vrmpy instructions only and no
activation vector load. That form of vrmpy takes an unsigned vector, thus the dot makes the
weights unsigned and subtracts the sum of the k-tile with the offset of the format: 8 for the
nibbles of Q4_0, and 128 for the bytes of Q8_0. The integer sums stay exact, thus a row gives the
result of the kernel of one row. The quantizer of the operator writes the compact copy and the
sums next to the tiled blocks, in the DDR scratchpad of the context.

The measurement of the lab, in cycles for one tile of 32 weight rows:

    rows        Q4_0 before   Q4_0 after    Q8_0 before   Q8_0 after
    1           70.8          51.1          ---           ---
    2           100.7         83.0          ---           ---
    3           171.4         89.4          ---           ---
    4           201.3         101.6         ---           ---

GGML_HEXAGON_MULTIROW=0 gives the operator the row-pair path of the checkout, thus one build
measures both. The operator keeps the row-pair path when the DDR scratchpad is too small for the
compact activation, and for every weight format other than Q4_0 and Q8_0.

